<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-each-element-multiple-functions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#order> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-each-element-multiple-functions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#source> "Hemenway, T. Gaia's Garden, 2nd ed., p. 6." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-each-element-multiple-functions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> "Jeff reuses patterns he invented (briefs, demos, gates) across new problems rather than inventing new abstractions per problem. Compresses rather than proliferates." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-each-element-multiple-functions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> "Each role carries several functions (Wren = PM + moderator + interaction-layer owner; Kade = engineer + gate-code + gate-quality; Silas = architect + ops + repo-infra). Each primitive serves multiple skills (chorus-log, git-queue.sh, nudge). Stack in time: briefs become stories become principles." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-each-element-multiple-functions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#label> "Each element performs multiple functions" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-each-element-multiple-functions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#comment> "Choose and place each element in a design so that it performs as many functions as possible. Beneficial connections between diverse components create a stable whole. Stack elements in both space and time." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-each-element-multiple-functions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ownedBy> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
