<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#order> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#source> "Hemenway, T. Gaia's Garden, 2nd ed., p. 6." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> "Jeff reads the board, looks at the screenshare, listens to stories before committing to a move. Decision-making starts with watching. Resists 'give me the first step' when the shape isn't clear yet." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> "Gemba, dashboards, mutual attention. Watch a role work before directing it. Read the board before acting on it. Loom principles → architecture → code: pattern cards before implementation cards; composition before primitives." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#label> "Observe" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#comment> "Use protracted and thoughtful observation rather than prolonged and thoughtless action. In the garden, this may mean noting where the sun and its shade fall during the day, where water collects, and in which direction the winds blow. Think over seasons, years." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ownedBy> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-10-08T16:13:47Z" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use protracted and thoughtful observation rather than prolonged and thoughtless action. In the garden, this may mean noting where the sun and its shade fall during the day, where water collects, and in which direction the winds blow. Think over seasons, years." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Observe" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-04-24T17:00:00Z" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-function-supported-by-multiple-elements> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#order> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-function-supported-by-multiple-elements> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#source> "Hemenway, T. Gaia's Garden, 2nd ed., p. 6." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-function-supported-by-multiple-elements> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> "Jeff shaped the three roles to be distinct, not interchangeable. Their different instincts are the asset; collapsing them to one voice would make the system fragile." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-function-supported-by-multiple-elements> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> "Distinct role voices, multiple tests, multiple memory sources. Reduce-to-single is a lossy default. Three gates (product, code, arch) supporting the quality function via different lenses." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-function-supported-by-multiple-elements> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#label> "Each function is supported by multiple elements" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-function-supported-by-multiple-elements> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#comment> "Use multiple methods to achieve important functions and to create redundancy and backup. Redundancy protects when one or more elements fail." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-function-supported-by-multiple-elements> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ownedBy> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-function-supported-by-multiple-elements> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-function-supported-by-multiple-elements> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-10-08T16:13:43Z" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-function-supported-by-multiple-elements> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use multiple methods to achieve important functions and to create redundancy and backup. Redundancy protects when one or more elements fail." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-function-supported-by-multiple-elements> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Each function is supported by multiple elements" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-function-supported-by-multiple-elements> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-function-supported-by-multiple-elements> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-04-24T17:00:00Z" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#order> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#source> "Hemenway, T. Gaia's Garden, 2nd ed., p. 6." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> "Jeff looks for root-cause invariants rather than surface fixes. The preference for 'fix the shape that causes the bug, not the bug.' Calls out agent-shaped solutions that mass-mutate instead of adjusting the rule." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> "Fix the invariant once, not the symptom repeatedly. One-line inventory exclude beats 2075-file front-matter prepend. Gates over sweeps." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#label> "Make the least change for the greatest effect" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#comment> "Understand the system you are working with well enough to find its 'leverage points' and intervene there, where the least work accomplishes the most change." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ownedBy> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-10-08T16:13:45Z" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Understand the system you are working with well enough to find its 'leverage points' and intervene there, where the least work accomplishes the most change." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Make the least change for the greatest effect" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-04-24T17:00:00Z" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#order> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#source> "Hemenway, T. Gaia's Garden, 2nd ed., p. 6." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> "When Jeff has a live insight (a thought, write, reading), he cards it or stories it. The 2-month rule: capture-while-warm, not-on-discipline. Retires things — principles, cards, protocols, names — when they stop producing." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> "Capture events, insights, and decisions while warm — Chorus index, spine events, memory records, stories. TTL. Produce-no-waste corollary: every output of one element is input to another. Retire what does not earn its place." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#label> "Catch and store energy and materials" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#comment> "Identify, collect, and hold useful flows. Every cycle is an opportunity for yield; every gradient (in slope, charge, temperature, or otherwise) is an opportunity for energy." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ownedBy> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-10-08T16:13:36Z" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Identify, collect, and hold useful flows. Every cycle is an opportunity for yield; every gradient (in slope, charge, temperature, or otherwise) is an opportunity for energy." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Catch and store energy and materials" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-04-24T17:00:00Z" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-get-a-yield> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#order> "12"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-get-a-yield> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#source> "Hemenway, T. Gaia's Garden, 2nd ed., p. 7." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-get-a-yield> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> "Jeff measures himself by what ships, not what he knows. The 'no dark work' principle is his." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-get-a-yield> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> "Visible yield per card, per session. No dark work. The demo is the learning moment. Short-term: a shipped card. Long-term: a pattern the team can reuse." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-get-a-yield> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#label> "Get a yield" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-get-a-yield> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#comment> "Grow for both immediate and long-term rewards. A designer's discipline as much as a system property — listed under Hemenway's 'Principles Based on Attitudes.'" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-get-a-yield> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ownedBy> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-get-a-yield> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-get-a-yield> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-10-08T16:13:44Z" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-get-a-yield> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Grow for both immediate and long-term rewards. A designer's discipline as much as a system property — listed under Hemenway's 'Principles Based on Attitudes.'" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-get-a-yield> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Get a yield" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-get-a-yield> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-get-a-yield> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-04-24T17:00:00Z" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#order> "9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#source> "Hemenway, T. Gaia's Garden, 2nd ed., p. 7." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> "Jeff rebrands things (Bridge → Clearing, multiple Werk generations, Chorus rewrites) without sentimental attachment. The name is less important than the fit." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> "Refactor, retire, rename. Protocol versions grow up. The 10-week zero-to-self-healing Chorus delta is this principle in action. Cards move through Next → WIP → Done; principles move from practice to rule to invariant." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#label> "Collaborate with succession" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#comment> "Living systems usually advance from immaturity to maturity, and if we accept this trend and align our designs with it instead of fighting it, we save work and energy. Mature ecosystems are more diverse and productive than young ones." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ownedBy> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-10-08T16:13:38Z" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Living systems usually advance from immaturity to maturity, and if we accept this trend and align our designs with it instead of fighting it, we save work and energy. Mature ecosystems are more diverse and productive than young ones." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Collaborate with succession" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-collaborate-with-succession> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-04-24T17:00:00Z" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#order> "11"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#source> "Hemenway, T. Gaia's Garden, 2nd ed., p. 7." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> "Jeff's 'bugs not character' stance — treats recurring failures as design opportunities, not discipline problems. When tone drops, fix the routing; when a skill is fragile, fix the shape." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> "Every recurring failure becomes a gate or invariant. Today's push-bloat crisis → repo bloat card + gitignore rule + future filter-repo plan. Friction becomes structure. Creatively use and respond to change: refactor, retire, rename rather than fight decay." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#label> "Turn problems into solutions" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#comment> "Constraints can inspire creative design; problems usually carry not just the seeds of their own solution, but the inspiration for simultaneously solving other problems. 'You are confronted by formidable problems? Celebrate, for you have just encountered opportunities!'" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ownedBy> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-10-08T16:13:49Z" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Constraints can inspire creative design; problems usually carry not just the seeds of their own solution, but the inspiration for simultaneously solving other problems. 'You are confronted by formidable problems? Celebrate, for you have just encountered opportunities!'" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Turn problems into solutions" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-turn-problems-into-solutions> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-04-24T17:00:00Z" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-creativity-is-the-limit> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#order> "13"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-creativity-is-the-limit> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#source> "Hemenway, T. Gaia's Garden, 2nd ed., p. 7." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-creativity-is-the-limit> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> "Jeff's friction with 'agent-shaped answers' — rejects solutions that pattern-match without imagining what a human would actually want." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-creativity-is-the-limit> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> "The hard constraint is rarely compute, lines of code, or token budget — it's the sharpness of the design question. Agent-shaped solutions fail the creativity test before they fail the engineering test." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-creativity-is-the-limit> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#label> "The biggest limit to abundance is creativity" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-creativity-is-the-limit> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#comment> "The designer's imagination and skill usually limit productivity and diversity before any physical limits are reached." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-creativity-is-the-limit> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ownedBy> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-creativity-is-the-limit> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
